To find each value of $\maroonD y$, we need to take each value of $\greenD x$ and $\blueD{\text{divide}}$ it $\blueD{\text{by } 2} $.

For example, when $\greenD {x} = \greenD{8}$:

$\begin{align}
\maroonD {y} &=\blueD{\dfrac{\greenD{8}}{2}} \\\\
\maroonD {y}&=\maroonD{4}
\end{align}$

To find the value of $\greenD{x}$, multiply both sides of the equation by $2$:

$\begin{align}
\maroonD{3} \blueD{\times2}&=\blueD{\dfrac{\greenD x}{2} \times2} \\\\
\greenD{6} &= \greenD{x}
\end{align}$
